<p>Includes an after-tax charge of $480 ($.09/share) to cover a revised estimate for remediation of the company's former manufacturing site in Carlstadt, N.J. (b) Includes an after-tax charge of $187 ($.04/share) in final settlement of a complaint by the U.S. Department of Justice sent to the company on Feb. 10, 1995.  The complaint alleged violation of the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA) by a then wholly owned subsidiary in Waterbury, Conn.  This subsidiary was sold on June 19, 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
